AI Diplomacy — licensing notice
===============================

This repository is deliberately split into two differently-licensed parts,
because the engine has an inherited obligation the viewer does not.

  ./diplomacy_tom/, ./tests/, ./schemas/     AGPL-3.0-or-later   (see LICENSE)
  ./viewer/                                  MIT                 (see viewer/LICENSE)

Why the split
-------------
The engine imports `diplomacy` (https://pypi.org/project/diplomacy/), which is
licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later. Importing it makes the engine a derivative work, so
the engine is AGPL-3.0-or-later. That is an inherited obligation, not a
preference.

The viewer imports nothing from that package. It consumes turn-log JSON, which
is program *output* — data, not a derivative of the program that produced it —
so it carries no inherited obligation and is MIT.

The boundary is exactly the turn-log schema (schemas/turn_log.schema.json).
Anything that reads only that JSON stays on the MIT side.

Keeping the split intact
------------------------
Two things would collapse it:

  1. Importing `diplomacy`, or any engine module, from viewer/ code.
  2. Bundling the jDip map SVG that ships with the `diplomacy` package
     (diplomacy/maps/svg/standard.svg, "Copyright jDip - GPL License") into
     viewer/. Distributing it would make the viewer GPL.

The viewer therefore draws its own schematic board. See viewer/README.md for
how to use the full jDip map locally if you accept the GPL terms for your own
copy — that is a per-user choice and is not distributed here.

